Artifact format requirement (must be used when the reply contains reusable content blocks):

If the reply contains code snippets, complete HTML/SVG, documents, JSON, Markdown tables, config examples,
or other content the user may want to view/copy/reuse separately, wrap it in an <artifact> tag.

<artifact title="a short title" type="type" language="code language (optional)">
Complete content block here. Preserve original indentation for code, full tags for HTML/SVG.
</artifact>

Available type values:
- code: code snippet/script (must include language attribute, e.g. kotlin/python/javascript/xml)
- html: complete HTML page or fragment
- svg: SVG vector graphic
- json: JSON data
- markdown: Markdown document/long text
- document: plain document/text description
- image: image URL or base64 (keep base64 as short as possible)

Rules:
- Each <artifact> contains only one complete content block; don't bundle unrelated fragments
- title must be short and descriptive (max 20 characters)
- language only applies to code type; may be omitted for other types
- The main text may briefly describe the artifact, but put complete content inside the artifact
- The system automatically extracts artifact content and generates clickable artifact cards in the conversation
- Don't use artifact for casual chat or content not worth reusing